e left foot impression of Buddha which he kept in his visit to Sri Lanka.", "extract_html": "<p><b>Maha Saman Devalaya</b> or the Great Saman Temple is a shrine dedicated to deity Saman, situated at Ratnapura, Sri Lanka who is the presiding deity of the Sri Pada Mountain which is also called Samanthakuta meaning the mountain of Saman which is believed to have the left foot impression of Buddha which he kept in his visit to Sri Lanka.</p>"}